    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## I.LPRF — LP report 138 \"Appointment Stats by Sales Rep with Source\" (thin transport ONLY)\n\nGmail (one trigger per month + the recurring current-month one) → keep CSV attachments\n→ POST raw CSV bytes → LP-MCP. ZERO parsing here.\n\n**One trigger per month is REQUIRED.** A single broad subject match does not pull the\nactual report — the month must be in the query. Same pattern as I.LPRB.\nEvery trigger must carry `downloadAttachments: true` in `options` or the message\narrives with no attachment.\n\n**Do NOT add a `_138_` filename regex.** CSV attachments are `_<YYMMDDHHMMSS>_Export.csv`\nwith no report id. Report identity is decided by LP-MCP's HEADER FINGERPRINT.\n\n**Route slug is a HINT, not the answer.** This posts to the `sales-efficiency` slug and\nLP-MCP re-routes it to `appt_stats_by_rep_source` from the header. That is by design —\n`detectReportFromHeader` is authoritative — and it is why report 138 has no slug of its\nown in `CSV_REPORT_TYPES`.\n\n**`?source=n8n` is load-bearing (added 2026-08-12).** The freshness watchdog arms a\nreport type only after one ingest logged with `source='n8n'`; the route defaults to\n`'manual'`. Without the parameter this feed ingests daily and is never guarded — if it\nstops, nothing alerts. Do not drop it.\n\n**Body mode is `binaryData` and that is deliberate.** It works here because the explicit\n`Content-Type: text/csv` header survives and LP-MCP's `express.text` parser accepts the\npayload. The sibling workflows decode to `csv_text` and post raw instead; both are live\nand both work. Do not \"harmonise\" this without testing it.\n\n**Failure handling.** 200 + `success:false` = deterministic rejection, never retried.\n`duplicate:true` is BENIGN and must not page — the IF passes it. 5xx = transport,\nretried 3×, then reported to `/events/lp_report_ingest_failed`.\n\n**Publish after import:** n8n activates the published version, not the autosaved draft.",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 1120
      },
      "id": "c7dfaf74-f3c7-4dc5-ac35-b2f0892bbdda",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
